WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.500
Is "Shazam! Fury of the Gods" a&nbsp;
"fun-filled" follow-up or just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.880
a "muddy mess"? Early reviews are in&nbsp;
– here's what DC fans should expect.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:14.520
The soon-to-be-retooled DC Universe is&nbsp;
attracting a fair amount of attention these days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:19.200
with fans wondering what direction James Gunn&nbsp;
and Peter Safran will take the struggling brand.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.300
Would they want to compete directly with the MCU&nbsp;
and offer lighthearted fare for the whole family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:29.160
or would they double down on the dark and&nbsp;
gritty as it had done previously? Or perhaps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.980
would they finally figure out&nbsp;
how to successfully mix both?

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:36.960
As such, all eyes are on the upcoming "Shazam!&nbsp;
Fury of the Gods" movie, which is a direct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:42.120
sequel to "Shazam!" While the film, alongside "The&nbsp;
Flash," was created before the decision to rework&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:47.823
the DCU, Safran is the producer and the film could&nbsp;
be a sign of what's in store for DC's future.

00:00:47.823 --> 00:00:52.860
The original 2019 movie was praised for&nbsp;
its tone and for its general sense of fun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:57.840
and some wondered if the sequel would be able to&nbsp;
capture this lightning in a bottle once again. Now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.940
that some early reactions are in for "Shazam!&nbsp;
Fury of the Gods," it looks like DC may have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:06.960
rare hit on their hands, which certainly&nbsp;
is a promising sign for what is to come.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.360
Critics and others who have&nbsp;
been given the privilege of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:13.140
seeing "Shazam! Fury of the Gods"&nbsp;
early have already started to heap&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:16.860
praise on the movie via Twitter.&nbsp;
John Nguyen of Nerd Reactor posted,

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:21.420
"'Shazam: Fury of the Gods' is a fun-filled&nbsp;
adventure that's a solid follow-up to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:27.000
first film. There is plenty of humor, action,&nbsp;
and heart, and it's always a treat to see the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.780
family together again. I wish the movie was&nbsp;
longer since there are a lot of characters."

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:35.820
Cinema Blend's Eric Eisenberg also felt&nbsp;
the same way and wrote that "Fury of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:40.440
Gods" is a super fun and worthy sequel to&nbsp;
the original film. He added that although&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:43.860
the "Shazam!" sequel isn't a movie that&nbsp;
will forever change comic book movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:48.000
it is still a great film filled with energy&nbsp;
and exceptionally likable characters.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.440
Shahbaz from The Movie Podcast could barely&nbsp;
contain his feelings about the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:55.620
claiming that it is the most fun he's&nbsp;
have ever had at the movie theater,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:59.040
and specifically praised the&nbsp;
performances of Helen Mirren,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:03.720
Lucy Liu, and Rachel Zegler as well as&nbsp;
the efforts of director David F. Sandberg.

00:02:03.841 --> 00:02:07.322
"The daughters of Atlas are coming to hunt us."

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:11.460
Jamie Broadnax of Black Girl Nerds&nbsp;
was another big fan, posting,

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:16.620
"Shazam continues to lean into his silliness&nbsp;
and immaturity in this sequel which tells us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:21.180
this franchise will remain to keep these&nbsp;
films funny, light and slapstick-ish. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:25.500
sequel comes with more action, compelling&nbsp;
villains and a complicated antihero."

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:29.640
Brandon Davis of ComicBook.com was&nbsp;
also pleased with the movie, writing,

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:35.340
"It's a really good sequel. The theme of found&nbsp;
family delivers great emotional beats. Sandberg&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:38.940
sprinkles some horror elements while&nbsp;
maintaining the childish joy &amp; charm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:43.140
of the Shazamily. Nothing brand new but&nbsp;
highly entertaining! Really enjoyed [it]."

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:46.380
Variety's Courtney Howard said&nbsp;
that the sequel packs a punch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:50.880
adding that it delivers on all fronts.&nbsp;
MTV's Tyrell Charles was a little more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:54.960
critical in his review and said that&nbsp;
even though "Shazam 2" is entertaining,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:59.760
it is very much a standard-issue superhero film&nbsp;
with a third act that drags on a little bit.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:05.520
Digital Spy's Gabriella Geisinger probably had&nbsp;
the spiciest opinion so far by saying that "Fury&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:10.260
of the Gods" only has a few bright spots and&nbsp;
that the third act is a muddy mess. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:14.220
most early reviewers have thoroughly&nbsp;
enjoyed "Shazam 2" so it will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:19.452
interesting to see how general audiences&nbsp;
react to this latest offering from DC.

